Hi Miguel,

Q1. You need to specify which site-level covariates you want to model.
For example:

fm <- colext(psiformula=~1, gammaformula=~x1, epsilonformula=~x1,
pformula=~1, data=umf)

Q2. If it does turn out that p=1, it would be nice to be able to fix
the parameter. Unfortunately that is not currently possible in
unmarked and I doubt that I will have time to add that feature anytime
soon.

Q3. You can get the expected values of colonization or extinction using predict:

predict(fm, type="col") # or type="ext"

Or you could do it "by hand":

plogis(model.matrix(~x1, site.covs) %*% coef(fm, type="col"))

Richard

