MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Giancarlo,

This is probably an issue related to the calculation of SEs using the delta method in linearComb(). Note that predict (source code is here <https://github.com/rbchan/unmarked/blob/master/R/unmarkedFit.R#L178>) is basically just a wrapper around linearComb() and backTransform(), so you could try to use them directly.  Don't have time to dig into it now, but an alternative is get your predictions this way:

oc <- obsCovs(yourUMF)
X <- model.matrix(~cov1 + cov2 + etc..., oc) # design matrix
betas <- coef(yourFittedModel, type="det")
p <- plogis(X %*% betas)

If you want SEs and CIs, you could apply the delta method yourself, or use either nonparboot or parboot.

Hope this helps,
Richard

