Hi Mario,

If I understand you correctly, yes you can use site-specific covariates in the 'col' and 'ext' parts of the model. I encourage you to look at the help page (?colext) where this is documented with examples.

As for the species dependent question, I'm afraid I don't follow you. If you have data from multiple species, you need to analyze them separately, or fit a dynamic multi-species occupancy model, possibly using BUGS or JAGS. Andy Royle, Robert Dorazio, Marc Ke'ry, and Elise Zipken among other have written extensively about these models.

Richard

